<title>UK: German trade seeks free market grains at EU tender.</title>
<headline>German trade seeks free market grains at EU tender.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders bid for 14,000 tonnes of wheat, 32,000 tonnes of barley and 5,000 tonnes of rye at Thursday's EU open market grain export tender, the state grain intervention board BLE said by telephone from Frankfurt.</p>
<p>Bids were for refunds ranging from 0.01 to 7.49 Ecus for the wheat, 28.80-30.55 Ecus for the barley and at 37.50 Ecus for the rye.</p>
<p>The tender will be adjudicated on Thursday afternoon by the EU cereals management committee.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
